    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.surround\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nreporting another bug which is kinda related to reproducible steps as well:\r\n`tpope/vim-surround` removes whitespaces in place of tag and fix indentation of html tags\r\ntpope: \r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/27911493/9f8d0782-43d8-4c06-953e-18538f58f9a8)\r\nmini.surround:\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/27911493/bffca64b-e48f-4039-9e0e-e9823843d4de)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. open this html file: https://bpa.st/PTHQY\r\n2. move cursor to line `<main>` and tries to remove tag using `sdt`\r\n3. No surrounding 't' found within 20 lines and config.search_moethod = 'cover'\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nexpected to remove `<main>` which is on the same line of cursor\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nproduce errors",
