        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski thanks for quick response, what do you think about the bug (or issue) described in description?\r\n\r\nNot really sure I 100% understand it. What I can say is that by default 'mini.surround' deletes *only* what it considers to be left and right surroundings, nothing more. If you want an extended behavior which affect indentation, try setting [`config.respect_selection_type`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a3e19d7b7850e711485b8adde73ba44789f2cf6/doc/mini-surround.txt#L482) to `true`. It might work for your use case.",
